WEBVTT

00:00.570 --> 00:02.270
- [Instructor] We're told
that Hannah and Martine

00:02.270 --> 00:04.360
each got a plant for their home.

00:04.360 --> 00:06.460
Hannah measured that her plant grows,

00:06.460 --> 00:10.730
on average, 2 centimeters per week.

00:10.730 --> 00:13.570
Martine measured that her plant grows,

00:13.570 --> 00:18.330
on average, 3 millimeters per day.

00:18.330 --> 00:21.970
Which plant grows faster?

00:21.970 --> 00:23.260
Pause this video and see

00:23.260 --> 00:25.783
if you can figure that out on your own.

00:26.970 --> 00:28.960
All right, now let's go
through this together.

00:28.960 --> 00:30.020
So at first when you look at it,

00:30.020 --> 00:32.020
you might just compare 3 to 2

00:32.020 --> 00:34.460
and say, oh, 3 is larger than 2,

00:34.460 --> 00:37.330
therefore maybe Martine's
plant grows faster.

00:37.330 --> 00:39.890
And you would think that
until you look at the units.

00:39.890 --> 00:42.410
This is millimeters per day

00:42.410 --> 00:44.100
while for Hannah's plant

00:44.100 --> 00:45.830
it's in centimeters per week.

00:45.830 --> 00:47.620
So in order to really compare them

00:47.620 --> 00:49.870
we have to convert them to the same units

00:49.870 --> 00:52.410
in both length and time.

00:52.410 --> 00:54.480
So let's convert both of them,

00:54.480 --> 00:56.260
let's convert them both
to centimeters per week.

00:56.260 --> 00:57.740
You could just try to convert both of them

00:57.740 --> 00:58.840
to millimeters per day

00:58.840 --> 01:00.510
or I guess you could try
to convert both of them

01:00.510 --> 01:03.920
to meters per year, a third set of units,

01:03.920 --> 01:05.920
but centimeters per week seems reasonable

01:05.920 --> 01:08.870
since we already have
Hannah's plant rate at,

01:08.870 --> 01:09.720
so let me write this down.

01:09.720 --> 01:11.950
So Hannah, I'll just write H,

01:11.950 --> 01:16.340
grows at 2 centimeters per week.

01:16.340 --> 01:17.883
And then you have Martine,

01:21.120 --> 01:26.120
grows at an average of
3 millimeters per day.

01:28.640 --> 01:30.530
Now how do we convert
3 millimeters per day

01:30.530 --> 01:32.660
to centimeters per week?

01:32.660 --> 01:35.240
Well, first we could
convert the millimeters,

01:35.240 --> 01:37.630
actually, first, let's
convert the days into weeks.

01:37.630 --> 01:39.630
So how many days are there in a week?

01:39.630 --> 01:41.010
Well, there's 7 days in a week.

01:41.010 --> 01:43.320
So if we have how many
millimeters per day,

01:43.320 --> 01:45.960
if we wanted to know millimeters per week

01:45.960 --> 01:47.960
we would multiply times 7 days.

01:47.960 --> 01:49.030
So let me do that.

01:49.030 --> 01:52.230
So times 7 days

01:53.998 --> 01:55.823
in a week.

01:57.090 --> 01:58.790
That would get us,

01:58.790 --> 02:00.570
this would be equal to 3 times 7

02:00.570 --> 02:04.280
which is equal to 21 millimeters

02:06.230 --> 02:07.960
in a week.

02:07.960 --> 02:08.830
And you can see, actually,

02:08.830 --> 02:10.900
that the units cancel
out nicely like that,

02:10.900 --> 02:13.310
so you're left with millimeters a week.

02:13.310 --> 02:15.790
And that makes sense, 3 millimeters a day,

02:15.790 --> 02:17.810
you're able to do 7 times that in a week,

02:17.810 --> 02:19.400
21 millimeters a week.

02:19.400 --> 02:21.930
And then when you think
about 21 millimeters

02:21.930 --> 02:23.980
is how many centimeters?

02:23.980 --> 02:25.560
Well, we just have to remember

02:25.560 --> 02:28.980
that 1 centimeter is
equal to 10 millimeters,

02:28.980 --> 02:32.870
so if we wanna covert
this into centimeters,

02:32.870 --> 02:34.820
we essentially have to divide by 10.

02:34.820 --> 02:39.820
We could just say 1/10 of
a centimeter per millimeter

02:40.360 --> 02:41.480
and then that gets us,

02:41.480 --> 02:42.960
we could write it in different ways,

02:42.960 --> 02:43.900
but we could write this,

02:43.900 --> 02:46.360
and even here the units cancel out nicely,

02:46.360 --> 02:50.453
21 divided by 10 is 2.1
centimeters per week.

02:55.450 --> 02:57.300
Another way you could
have just thought about it

02:57.300 --> 03:02.300
is we could say 1 centimeter
is equal to 10 millimeters,

03:03.100 --> 03:05.577
or if you divide both sides by 10,

03:05.577 --> 03:10.570
1/10 of a centimeter is
equal to 1 millimeter,

03:10.570 --> 03:13.670
and if 1 millimeter is equal
to 1/10 of a centimeter

03:13.670 --> 03:18.310
then 21 millimeters is just
going to be 21 times this,

03:18.310 --> 03:21.700
21 times 1/10 is the same
thing as 21 divided by 10,

03:21.700 --> 03:26.063
it would be 2.1 centimeters.

03:27.340 --> 03:29.940
And so now we can compare
2.1 centimeters per week

03:29.940 --> 03:31.520
compared to 2 centimeters a week.

03:31.520 --> 03:32.353
Well, it turns out that

03:32.353 --> 03:36.100
when you actually compare
the appropriate units

03:36.100 --> 03:38.250
it still turns out that Martine's plant

03:38.250 --> 03:40.563
is growing just a little bit faster.
